Text: "The natural numbers formalize discrete iteration. They may be described
       abstractly by zero, successor, and induction, or realized concretely as
       the finite von Neumann ordinals. The first two pages develop those
       viewpoints; the final page isolates induction and recursion as the
       characteristic reasoning and construction principles of $\mathbb{N}$.
       The separation between abstract structure and concrete realization is
       deliberate: arithmetic theorems depend on the Peano structure, not on
       the accidental details of its set-theoretic encoding."
Id: "a338a613-ef12-4fab-9b9f-f0a9f6760515"
